{"id": "q_wolf_status", "question": "End of Session 12: is the Wolf alive, dead, still corrupted-what's his state?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at the end of Session 12—Bonogo “Removed the Wolf’s head to take it to the academy,” which is a terminal outcome.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: Dead (OBSERVED)\n- Cause: Decapitation by Bonogo (OBSERVED: “Removed the Wolf’s head to take it to the academy”)\n- Corruption: Previously corrupted/linked to the cult (CANON: “The Wolf has been subtly leading key figures of the city guard into the cult’s fold”)\n- Current State: No longer active; terminally resolved\n\nExplanation:\nThe OBSERVED session recap provides a clear terminal outcome: Bonogo “Removed the Wolf’s head to take it to the academy.” This definitively establishes the Wolf as dead by the end of Session 12. While CANON establishes that the Wolf was corrupted and acting as an agent of the cult, that condition is no longer active post-decapitation. No conflicting OBSERVED facts suggest survival or transformation after this moment, so death is the current and authoritative state.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 66, "duration_ms": 53, "top_5": [["ent_eirik", 1.3478], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.1637], ["ent_torbin_jove", 1.0], ["ent_mercenaries", 0.9639], ["ent_city_guard", 0.8979]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_eirik", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_torbin_jove", "ent_mercenaries", "ent_city_guard", "ent_draven", "ent_speak_with_dead", "ent_lyra", "ent_zyla_cinderbranch", "ent_key", "ent_moment_of_decision", "ent_great_shepherd", "ent_divine_reflection_pool", "ent_seed", "ent_the_butcher", "ent_dead_gods_corrupted_flesh", "ent_corruption", "ent_fast_eyed_and_disarming", "ent_harvek", "ent_seren_darkroot", "ent_wolf", "ent_commander_thalia_ashenvale", "ent_insight", "ent_public_performer", "ent_dwarf", "ent_goblin", "ent_glowkindle", "ent_torrin_flamescale", "ent_baegrom", "ent_stafl", "ent_flames", "