{"id": "q_pre_post", "question": "Before vs after the council fight-how's the Wolf different?", "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf was an active manipulator embedded in the city’s power structure; after, he is definitively neutralized—“Removed the Wolf’s head to take it to the academy.”\n\n**Before the council fight (CANON + OBSERVED):**  \n- The Wolf was a key hidden actor within Mirathorn, “subtly leading key figures of the city guard into the cult’s fold” (the cult history).  \n- He functioned as an infiltrator and corrupter tied to the cult’s broader plans in the city.  \n- The council context suggests tension, hesitation, and possible internal corruption, which aligns with the Wolf’s influence operating behind the scenes.\n\n**After the council fight (OBSERVED):**  \n- The Wolf is no longer an active agent: Bonogo “Removed the Wolf’s head to take it to the academy.”  \n- This is a terminal outcome, indicating total removal rather than escape or ambiguity.  \n- Post-fight, any ongoing cult activity is no longer being directly guided by the Wolf, shifting the threat from centralized manipulation to remaining cult forces.\n\n**Key Attributes:**  \n- History: Led guard figures into the cult (CANON) → decapitated (OBSERVED)  \n- Role: Hidden manipulator → eliminated target  \n- Operational Status: Active infiltrator → terminated (“Removed the Wolf’s head to take it to the academy”)", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 65, "duration_ms": 46, "top_5": [["ent_eirik", 1.4565], ["ent_key", 1.2], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.1365], ["ent_city_guard", 1.0294], ["ent_commander_thalia_ashenvale", 1.0294]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_eirik", "ent_key", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_city_guard", "ent_commander_thalia_ashenvale", "ent_the_fight", "The_Shepherd_s_Council", "ent_council", "ent_secret_escape_tunnel", "ent_barns", "ent_copper_moss_brewery", "ent_painted_cloth_banner", "ent_tables", "scout"