{"id": "q_thalia", "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?", "answer": "TL;DR: There’s no direct evidence about Thalia in the projection; however, CANON indicates the Wolf has been subtly leading guard members into the cult, so if Thalia is a guard, she could plausibly be either corrupted or manipulated—but the data does not confirm which.\n\nBased on available facts:\n- CANON: The Wolf “has been subtly leading key figures of the city guard into the cult’s fold” (the cult history).\n- CANON/OBSERVED: The cult includes former guard members (cultists faction), and corruption/mind-altering influence is a recurring theme (trances, hallucination fumes, “corrupted” portrayal notes).\n\nThere is no mention of Thalia specifically, so:\n- It cannot be confirmed whether she was corrupted (mentally/physically altered) or merely manipulated (“played”).\n- Both are consistent with how the Wolf and cult operate.\n\nInterpretation constraint:\n- If Thalia was part of the Guard, the Wolf’s established method suggests a pipeline: influence → recruitment → possible corruption.\n- Without explicit mention, her exact state remains unresolved.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- the cult (faction)\n  - history: Wolf recruits from city guard\n  - methods: subtle manipulation, corruption, hallucination effects\n- cultists (npc)\n  - faction: former Guard members\n  - mental_state: trance, fear, reverence\n  - portrayal_notes: explicitly “Corrupted”", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 62, "duration_ms": 40, "top_5": [["ent_the_wolf", 1.48], ["ent_commander_thalia_ashenvale", 1.36], ["ent_thalia", 0.9453], ["ent_city_guard", 0.7371], ["ent_corruption", 0.7371]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_the_wolf", "ent_commander_thalia_ashenvale", "ent_thalia", "ent_city_guard", "ent_corruption", "ent_speak_with_dead", "ent_eirik", "ent_lute", "ent_draven", "ent_tie_the_vines_themselves", "ent_tie_